      "html": "<p>Before its scientific description this beautiful species of dwarf cichlid was known in the hobby as the \"Sunset-Apistogramma\". The body coloration of a female during brood care is reminiscent of a sunset. The scientific name, atahualpa, refers to the last great ruler of the Inka empire, Atahualpa. He was captured by the Spaniard Pizarro in 1532 and executed in 1533; this was the sunset of the Inka empire.</p>"
    },
